WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.074
Watch Online Movies and Series for FREE
www.osdb.link/lm

2
00:02:47.042 --> 00:02:49.294
Stop dilly-dallying. Big Brother.

3
00:02:49.378 --> 00:02:51.922
This yard sale isn't gonna set up itself.

4
00:02:52.840 --> 00:02:53.841
Coming. Sally.

5
00:03:06.645 --> 00:03:08.689
I love a spring yard sale.

6
00:03:08.772 --> 00:03:11.942
It's the perfect time
to get rid of all your old stuff

7
00:03:12.025 --> 00:03:14.152
to make room for new stuff.

8
00:03:15.320 --> 00:03:17.990
I'll be sad to see
some of these old things go.

9
00:03:18.699 --> 00:03:21.660
Hopefully. they'll make
someone else just as happy.

10
00:03:22.744 --> 00:03:26.290
Well. all the money we get
will make me happy.

11
00:03:26.373 --> 00:03:29.585
Snoopy. do you have anything
you'd like to sell?

12
00:03:30.210 --> 00:03:32.880
What can a dog have to sell
at a yard sale?

13
00:03:51.440 --> 00:03:53.400
Is that my hockey stick?

14
00:03:56.111 --> 00:03:58.447
I prefer a more curated approach.

15
00:03:58.530 --> 00:04:01.074
It's all about the presentation.

16
00:04:01.158 --> 00:04:04.703
Wow. there sure is
some great stuff in here.

17
00:04:05.329 --> 00:04:06.705
My old glove.

18
00:04:06.788 --> 00:04:10.042
I know it doesn't fit anymore.

19
00:04:10.125 --> 00:04:13.003
but it's full of memories.

20
00:04:13.086 --> 00:04:15.672
I almost made a game-winning catch
with this glove.

21
00:04:22.179 --> 00:04:25.265
So. it's really just a game-losing glove.

22
00:04:32.564 --> 00:04:34.483
We're open for business.

23
00:04:34.566 --> 00:04:35.984
Right this way.

24
00:04:36.610 --> 00:04:38.362
No pushing. no shoving.

25
00:04:38.445 --> 00:04:40.989
-There's plenty for everyone.
-Look. check it out!

26
00:04:47.454 --> 00:04:49.248
Classic Bunny Wunny.

27
00:04:49.831 --> 00:04:52.584
Nothing says spring like a new perfume.

28
00:04:52.668 --> 00:04:55.504
Wouldn't you agree. my Sweet Babboo?

29
00:04:55.587 --> 00:04:58.298
I'm not your Sweet Babboo.

30
00:04:58.382 --> 00:05:01.176
but I do love a fresh scent.

31
00:05:01.260 --> 00:05:03.053
What does it smell like?

32
00:05:03.136 --> 00:05:05.472
No idea. My mom donated them.

33
00:05:06.515 --> 00:05:09.518
This one is called. "Sample."

34
00:05:10.227 --> 00:05:13.730
It's pronounced "Sample." It's French.

35
00:05:22.030 --> 00:05:24.741
Do I detect a top note of jasmine?

36
00:05:24.825 --> 00:05:27.369
-Or is that…
-It's bubble gum. you blockhead.

37
00:05:27.452 --> 00:05:28.662
I'll take it.

38
00:05:30.455 --> 00:05:31.874
What else do you have?

39
00:05:32.457 --> 00:05:35.252
Vanilla pudding. rose bouquet. strawberry…

40
00:05:35.335 --> 00:05:36.587
I'll take them all.

41
00:05:37.421 --> 00:05:39.673
How much for this fishing pole. Sally?

42
00:05:40.674 --> 00:05:42.885
That's $1.35. Franklin.

43
00:05:42.968 --> 00:05:45.179
My grandpa always says.

44
00:05:45.262 --> 00:05:48.390
"You can't put a price
on a good day of fishing."

45
00:05:49.266 --> 00:05:50.767
How about a $1.20?

46
00:05:51.977 --> 00:05:53.020
Sold.

47
00:06:06.950 --> 00:06:08.535
Fifty cents?

48
00:06:08.619 --> 00:06:10.829
What am I? A millionaire?

49
00:06:12.831 --> 00:06:15.959
Hey. Snoopy. Does this accordion work?

50
00:06:25.677 --> 00:06:29.264
No. thanks.
My mom would just make me practice.

51
00:06:34.478 --> 00:06:37.397
Have it. Don't need it. Don't want it.

52
00:06:38.023 --> 00:06:39.441
Nope. Never.

53
00:06:40.108 --> 00:06:41.276
A waffle maker?

54
00:06:41.360 --> 00:06:43.737
I'm more of a pancake gal.

55
00:06:46.031 --> 00:06:48.659
Who painted this? A dog?

56
00:07:16.019 --> 00:07:19.940
I never realized
beagles were so sensitive.

57
00:07:23.569 --> 00:07:25.737
How much for this baseball card. Chuck?

58
00:07:26.947 --> 00:07:30.325
That one?
I didn't realize I put it in there.

59
00:07:30.409 --> 00:07:32.870
I should probably keep it.
Peppermint Patty.

60
00:07:32.953 --> 00:07:34.162
It's my favorite.

61
00:07:35.664 --> 00:07:37.207
How about this one?

62
00:07:39.459 --> 00:07:41.211
That's my other favorite.

63
00:07:42.713 --> 00:07:44.047
What about this ball?

64
00:07:44.131 --> 00:07:46.675
It looks like it's never even been hit.

65
00:07:46.758 --> 00:07:49.219
Actually. they're all my favorites.

66
00:07:49.928 --> 00:07:52.931
You sure have a funny way
of doing business. Chuck.

67
00:08:01.481 --> 00:08:05.694
Hey. Charles.
Is all this baseball gear really for sale?

68
00:08:06.236 --> 00:08:07.446
Hi. Milo.

69
00:08:08.780 --> 00:08:10.407
Funny you should mention that.

70
00:08:10.490 --> 00:08:12.284
Because my baseball team.

71
00:08:12.367 --> 00:08:15.329
we're called The Goose Eggs.
on account of how...

72
00:08:15.412 --> 00:08:17.414
You've never scored a run.

73
00:08:17.497 --> 00:08:18.832
I remember.

74
00:08:18.916 --> 00:08:20.751
I know how that feels.

75
00:08:23.921 --> 00:08:26.882
Maybe all you need
is a little more practice.

76
00:08:26.965 --> 00:08:28.675
It's kind of hard.

77
00:08:28.759 --> 00:08:31.053
Austin lost our only bat.

78
00:08:31.136 --> 00:08:34.847
And Ruby still uses
an oven mitt for a glove.

79
00:08:36.683 --> 00:08:39.394
This would be a major step up
for the team.

80
00:08:43.106 --> 00:08:44.441
How much?

81
00:08:45.943 --> 00:08:47.152
It's just…

82
00:08:52.074 --> 00:08:54.368
These are for display… only.

83
00:08:58.872 --> 00:09:01.834
It did seem too good to be true.

84
00:09:04.753 --> 00:09:07.756
Charlie Brown. you're the only kid I know

85
00:09:07.840 --> 00:09:10.968
who could have a yard sale
and not sell anything!

86
00:09:15.013 --> 00:09:16.682
That'll be ten cents.

87
00:09:17.349 --> 00:09:18.892
It served its purpose.

88
00:09:21.603 --> 00:09:25.148
Attention. shoppers. everything must go.

89
00:09:25.232 --> 00:09:27.568
No reasonable offer refused.

90
00:09:27.651 --> 00:09:28.694
Nice!

91
00:09:29.278 --> 00:09:30.279
Yes!

92
00:09:30.988 --> 00:09:32.656
Thank you. All sales final.

93
00:09:32.739 --> 00:09:34.032
Thanks. All sales final.

94
00:09:34.116 --> 00:09:36.034
Pleasure doing business with you.

95
00:09:36.118 --> 00:09:37.870
All sales final!

96
00:09:43.542 --> 00:09:45.335
You sold everything.

97
00:09:46.295 --> 00:09:47.713
Even the tables.

98
00:09:49.256 --> 00:09:51.592
I made a pretty penny too.

99
00:09:51.675 --> 00:09:54.219
I even sold an old dollhouse.

100
00:09:54.303 --> 00:09:56.805
I forgot I had an old dollhouse.

101
00:10:00.475 --> 00:10:03.812
Sally. you sold Snoopy's doghouse?

102
00:10:05.480 --> 00:10:06.982
Are you certain?

103
00:10:07.065 --> 00:10:09.860
I'm pretty sure I heard dollhouse.

104
00:10:15.157 --> 00:10:17.242
Do you remember who you sold it to?

105
00:10:20.537 --> 00:10:24.333
It's kinda hard to think
with all that noise.

106
00:10:29.046 --> 00:10:31.548
Sally! It's important.

107
00:10:31.632 --> 00:10:33.008
I don't remember.

108
00:10:33.091 --> 00:10:35.761
In the thrill of commerce.
it's all a blur.

109
00:10:36.887 --> 00:10:38.263
Poor Snoopy.

110
00:10:52.653 --> 00:10:57.324
People think that a lot could be said

111
00:10:57.407 --> 00:10:59.243
Welcome to your new home. Snoopy.

112
00:10:59.326 --> 00:11:02.955
About where it is you lay your head

113
00:11:03.789 --> 00:11:08.460
A big old house or a tin-roof shed

114
00:11:09.545 --> 00:11:14.758
But home is where your heart can rest

115
00:11:15.259 --> 00:11:19.721
Chandeliers or velvet drapes

116
00:11:21.223 --> 00:11:25.435
A big old table
And some porcelain plates

117
00:11:26.520 --> 00:11:31.024
I don't care how you fill your space

118
00:11:31.775 --> 00:11:37.030
You ain't home
Until your heart feels safe

119
00:11:37.114 --> 00:11:43.036
All of these memories
To share with my friends

120
00:11:43.120 --> 00:11:48.625
Warm autumn mornings or wintery winds

121
00:11:48.709 --> 00:11:54.381
Life is full of the stories we write

122
00:11:54.464 --> 00:11:56.550
Home's not a house

123
00:11:56.633 --> 00:11:59.845
It's a feeling inside

124
00:11:59.928 --> 00:12:05.100
Some say it's over the rainbow

125
00:12:06.059 --> 00:12:08.937
Deep inside of your dreams

126
00:12:09.021 --> 00:12:11.565
Deep inside your dreams

127
00:12:11.648 --> 00:12:16.486
But lucky for me
I'm where I'm supposed to be

128
00:12:17.362 --> 00:12:20.991
Home where your heart found me

129
00:12:23.035 --> 00:12:27.289
Riding bikes or hide and seek

130
00:12:28.290 --> 00:12:33.128
Well. it all means more
When you're here with me

131
00:12:34.213 --> 00:12:38.967
There's so many stories yet to be

132
00:12:39.051 --> 00:12:45.390
Oh. home is where your heart is free

133
00:12:45.474 --> 00:12:50.646
Some say it's over the rainbow

134
00:12:51.188 --> 00:12:53.941
Deep inside of your dreams

135
00:12:54.024 --> 00:12:56.693
Deep inside your dreams

136
00:12:56.777 --> 00:13:01.615
But lucky for me
I'm where I'm supposed to be

137
00:13:02.407 --> 00:13:06.036
Home where your heart found me

138
00:13:51.748 --> 00:13:53.625
Well. it is spring.

139
00:13:53.709 --> 00:13:57.004
Think of it as the perfect time
for a fresh start.

140
00:14:01.675 --> 00:14:04.720
Why don't we just go shopping
for a new doghouse?

141
00:14:15.522 --> 00:14:16.982
Don't worry. Snoopy.

142
00:14:17.065 --> 00:14:19.610
I'm sure we'll find something
you like in here.

143
00:14:20.152 --> 00:14:22.321
This store sells just about everything.

144
00:14:45.219 --> 00:14:46.220
Here they are.

145
00:14:51.934 --> 00:14:53.602
This one looks cozy.

146
00:14:58.357 --> 00:15:00.108
This one's festive.

147
00:15:11.286 --> 00:15:13.705
How about this one? It floats.

148
00:15:17.876 --> 00:15:21.046
Too cold.

149
00:15:22.339 --> 00:15:24.216
Maybe too contemporary.

150
00:15:25.509 --> 00:15:28.428
I'm surprised they can even
call this one a house.

151
00:15:34.935 --> 00:15:38.230
I'm sorry we couldn't find you
a new doghouse. Snoopy.

152
00:15:38.313 --> 00:15:40.858
If only we could figure out where it went.

153
00:15:40.941 --> 00:15:42.901
It's a real mystery.

154
00:15:56.540 --> 00:16:00.460
The real mystery is
why can't I have a normal dog?

155
00:16:05.841 --> 00:16:09.011
The world's greatest detective
is on the case.

156
00:16:27.487 --> 00:16:31.074
Ninety-eight. 99. 100.

157
00:16:31.158 --> 00:16:33.035
That's a personal best. sir.

158
00:16:33.702 --> 00:16:34.703
Yes!

159
00:16:39.416 --> 00:16:40.959
Sorry. Peppermint Patty.

160
00:16:41.043 --> 00:16:43.003
Snoopy thought you were a typewriter.

161
00:16:46.882 --> 00:16:49.384
I can never quite figure you out. Chuck.

162
00:17:34.263 --> 00:17:37.015
All hail the bubble king!

163
00:17:44.898 --> 00:17:49.945
Is that the scent of freshly baked
chocolate chip cookies?

164
00:17:59.288 --> 00:18:01.081
Save me one. Snoopy.

165
00:18:02.374 --> 00:18:03.500
Your Majesty.

166
00:18:19.892 --> 00:18:21.268
Watch it. beagle!

167
00:18:23.395 --> 00:18:25.564
What is the meaning of this?

168
00:18:25.647 --> 00:18:28.233
He's following the scent
of chocolate chip cookies.

169
00:18:28.317 --> 00:18:30.319
You must mean my new perfume.

170
00:18:30.402 --> 00:18:32.237
I got it at your yard sale.

171
00:18:32.779 --> 00:18:34.323
Take a sniff.

172
00:18:36.825 --> 00:18:39.745
Yep. freshly baked chocolate chip cookies.

173
00:18:43.373 --> 00:18:45.167
I've been licked by a dog!

174
00:18:45.250 --> 00:18:48.212
Get the iodine. Call animal services.

175
00:18:48.295 --> 00:18:50.631
Germs. germs. germs!

176
00:19:07.773 --> 00:19:10.192
At least it turned out to be a nice day.

177
00:19:17.449 --> 00:19:20.619
Sorry. I shouldn't have said that.

178
00:19:20.702 --> 00:19:22.913
It hasn't been a nice day for you.

179
00:19:25.374 --> 00:19:29.086
Maybe it would help to think
of something else. like baseball.

180
00:19:29.628 --> 00:19:31.880
That always makes me feel better.

181
00:19:31.964 --> 00:19:36.009
I imagine pitching a perfect game
or catching a fly ball.

182
00:19:36.093 --> 00:19:37.636
Or sliding into home.

183
00:19:42.432 --> 00:19:43.851
Did I say home?

184
00:19:45.894 --> 00:19:47.855
I can't say anything right.

185
00:19:50.941 --> 00:19:55.028
Snoopy. I know your doghouse
means the world to you.

186
00:19:55.112 --> 00:19:58.824
We're going to get it back
no matter how long it takes.

187
00:19:58.907 --> 00:19:59.992
All spring.

188
00:20:00.075 --> 00:20:05.247
Into summer. fall. winter. night. day.

189
00:20:05.330 --> 00:20:06.707
Even recess.

190
00:20:22.514 --> 00:20:26.018
Just remember. we're in this together.

191
00:20:37.487 --> 00:20:39.323
Snoopy. wait.

192
00:20:39.406 --> 00:20:41.658
Let's not jump to any conclusions.

193
00:20:46.413 --> 00:20:47.998
Hello. Charles.

194
00:20:50.792 --> 00:20:56.131
Milo? Earlier today
you were at our yard sale.

195
00:20:56.215 --> 00:20:59.510
That was a very good yard sale. Charles.

196
00:20:59.593 --> 00:21:00.719
Thank you. Milo.

197
00:21:00.802 --> 00:21:02.930
Did you happen to buy anything?

198
00:21:03.013 --> 00:21:04.264
I sure did.

199
00:21:07.476 --> 00:21:09.478
I got a whole box of stuff.

200
00:21:11.355 --> 00:21:16.652
I bought some comic books
and a jigsaw puzzle and a bicycle horn.

201
00:21:18.737 --> 00:21:20.405
I bought some macaroni art.

202
00:21:21.698 --> 00:21:26.119
Two hair bows for Ruby.
They were buy one get one free.

203
00:21:26.203 --> 00:21:28.038
Let's see. What else?

204
00:21:28.121 --> 00:21:29.706
What about a doghouse?

205
00:21:29.790 --> 00:21:31.166
Or a dollhouse.

206
00:21:31.250 --> 00:21:34.795
Did you happen to buy either of those
from my sister Sally?

207
00:21:35.295 --> 00:21:36.296
No.

208
00:21:36.922 --> 00:21:39.424
But I did get something much better.

209
00:21:42.469 --> 00:21:46.223
It's the Goose Eggs'
official new clubhouse!

210
00:22:00.279 --> 00:22:01.280
Hey!

211
00:22:03.574 --> 00:22:05.200
Do you want a tour?

212
00:22:05.701 --> 00:22:07.119
I love this place!

213
00:22:07.202 --> 00:22:10.497
The thing is. this is Snoopy's doghouse.

214
00:22:10.581 --> 00:22:11.582
It is?

215
00:22:12.082 --> 00:22:13.917
Sally wasn't supposed to sell it.

216
00:22:14.459 --> 00:22:15.711
It was a mistake.

217
00:22:16.378 --> 00:22:19.214
Do you think there's any way
I could get it back?

218
00:22:19.298 --> 00:22:20.883
Are you kidding me?

219
00:22:20.966 --> 00:22:22.676
Look at the Goose Eggs.

220
00:22:22.759 --> 00:22:26.471
This clubhouse is the best thing
that ever happened to us.

221
00:22:27.181 --> 00:22:29.933
Plus. I have a receipt from your sister.

222
00:22:30.017 --> 00:22:33.478
-I want to live here forever.
-"All sales final."

223
00:22:53.957 --> 00:22:55.292
Please. Milo.

224
00:22:55.375 --> 00:22:57.711
There must be something I can do.

225
00:22:57.794 --> 00:22:59.421
Sorry. Charles.

226
00:22:59.505 --> 00:23:01.798
It wouldn't be fair to the team.

227
00:23:45.342 --> 00:23:47.094
Everything okay. Charlie Brown?

228
00:23:47.678 --> 00:23:49.429
I'm afraid not. Franklin.

229
00:23:50.013 --> 00:23:53.183
It's Snoopy. We lost his doghouse.

230
00:23:54.810 --> 00:23:56.311
You had me worried there.

231
00:23:57.813 --> 00:23:58.814
What do you mean?

232
00:23:59.398 --> 00:24:02.359
Don't get me wrong. it's a big deal.

233
00:24:02.442 --> 00:24:04.820
But it's not the end of the world.

234
00:24:05.696 --> 00:24:07.990
I'm not sure Snoopy would agree.

235
00:24:08.949 --> 00:24:10.534
Houses are important.

236
00:24:10.617 --> 00:24:13.537
but they're made
from wood. nails and bricks.

237
00:24:14.079 --> 00:24:17.916
Also concrete. stone. a variety of metals…

238
00:24:19.710 --> 00:24:23.297
The point is.
those things are all replaceable.

239
00:24:23.380 --> 00:24:25.591
Whenever I've moved houses.

240
00:24:25.674 --> 00:24:29.803
I found the important things
always have a way of coming with me.

241
00:24:29.887 --> 00:24:32.472
My memories. my family.

242
00:24:32.556 --> 00:24:35.142
That's what home is to me. Charlie Brown.

243
00:24:37.769 --> 00:24:40.731
You just need to know
what's worth holding on to.

244
00:24:41.440 --> 00:24:44.234
-Everything else is just…
-Stuff.

245
00:24:45.527 --> 00:24:48.238
Good advice.
Did your grandpa tell you that?

246
00:24:48.947 --> 00:24:51.366
I read it on the back of a cereal box.

247
00:24:53.285 --> 00:24:54.286
Thanks. Franklin.

248
00:25:00.501 --> 00:25:04.546
Hey. I knew that was
around here somewhere.

249
00:25:04.630 --> 00:25:07.591
Let me know
if you catch a set of encyclopedias.

250
00:25:12.179 --> 00:25:14.973
Fifty-six. 57…

251
00:25:15.057 --> 00:25:17.768
Who knew spring-cleaning could be so fun?

252
00:25:18.268 --> 00:25:20.312
And profitable.

253
00:25:20.395 --> 00:25:23.982
Now remember.
always count the quarters first

254
00:25:24.066 --> 00:25:26.068
because they're the easiest to stack.

255
00:25:31.490 --> 00:25:33.408
Wow.

256
00:25:34.076 --> 00:25:37.663
Are you sure you want to
give all this up. Charles?

257
00:25:38.247 --> 00:25:40.791
I'm not sure of a lot of things. Milo.

258
00:25:40.874 --> 00:25:44.378
But I know there's nothing
I wouldn't give up for my dog.

259
00:25:44.962 --> 00:25:46.296
Do we have a deal?

260
00:25:48.590 --> 00:25:49.675
Deal.

261
00:25:53.804 --> 00:25:56.932
I hope the Goose Eggs
have as much fun with it as I did.

262
00:25:58.267 --> 00:25:59.434
Dibs on the bat.

263
00:25:59.518 --> 00:26:01.812
-This glove has fingers.
-Hooray!

264
00:26:03.814 --> 00:26:05.065
Perfect fit.

265
00:26:05.649 --> 00:26:06.775
Play ball.

266
00:26:10.696 --> 00:26:11.822
Almost.

267
00:26:11.905 --> 00:26:13.282
Go long. Leland.

268
00:26:13.365 --> 00:26:14.783
I got it. I got it.

269
00:26:19.288 --> 00:26:20.998
I almost got it.

270
00:26:21.081 --> 00:26:22.583
Hooray. Yay.

271
00:26:22.666 --> 00:26:24.501
Big leagues. here we come.

272
00:26:50.777 --> 00:26:53.447
Nice to see your house
back where it belongs.

273
00:26:53.530 --> 00:26:56.575
With a few fixes. it'll be as good as new.

274
00:27:16.303 --> 00:27:18.347
I'm so sorry. Snoopy.

275
00:27:19.515 --> 00:27:22.768
But there's nothing here
we can't repair or replace.

276
00:27:23.727 --> 00:27:26.563
A home is made
from the memories you create

277
00:27:26.647 --> 00:27:28.398
and the people you love.

278
00:27:29.191 --> 00:27:32.903
And no matter how many times
you lose your house.

279
00:27:32.986 --> 00:27:36.198
you'll always have a home with me.
old pal.

280
00:27:38.283 --> 00:27:39.493
And me.

281
00:27:40.035 --> 00:27:46.708
After all. there's an argument to be made
that some small part of this is my fault.

282
00:27:47.251 --> 00:27:49.127
I got you covered. Snoopy.

283
00:27:49.211 --> 00:27:50.212
Me too.

284
00:27:50.295 --> 00:27:51.880
We're here for you. Snoopy.

285
00:27:51.964 --> 00:27:53.465
I wouldn't miss it.

286
00:27:53.549 --> 00:27:55.092
You have my scrubber.

287
00:27:55.634 --> 00:27:57.636
All right. all right!

288
00:27:59.179 --> 00:28:01.181
I guess I'll supervise.

289
00:28:08.897 --> 00:28:13.151
No matter where I sleep tonight

290
00:28:14.278 --> 00:28:16.530
Your love is always

291
00:28:16.613 --> 00:28:18.991
Tucking me in tight

292
00:28:19.867 --> 00:28:24.454
Friends are there
To keep you shining bright

293
00:28:25.330 --> 00:28:29.793
Home is where your heart feels light

294
00:28:31.128 --> 00:28:36.800
Some say it's over the rainbow

295
00:28:36.884 --> 00:28:39.803
Deep inside of your dreams

296
00:28:39.887 --> 00:28:42.848
Deep inside your dreams

297
00:28:42.931 --> 00:28:47.603
But lucky for me
I'm where I'm supposed to be

298
00:28:48.353 --> 00:28:51.190
Home where your heart found

299
00:28:51.273 --> 00:28:55.861
Some say it's over the rainbow

300
00:28:56.570 --> 00:29:01.241
Deep inside of your dreams

301
00:29:02.159 --> 00:29:06.872
But lucky for me
I am where I'm supposed to be

302
00:29:08.081 --> 00:29:13.712
Home where your heart found me

303
00:29:13.795 --> 00:29:15.756
Welcome home. Snoopy.

304
00:29:31.855 --> 00:29:34.983
Don't forget. we're in this together.

305
00:30:19.778 --> 00:30:23.323
This wasn't exactly
what I meant by together.

305
